package core

const directiveStateContract = "The directive says what should remain true. Conversation history, recalled memory, and tool records say what already happened. Never use the directive as a run log."

const recurringDirectiveContract = "For recurring work, persist only the responsibility and cadence exactly as the owner stated. Do not invent calendar details or store run dates, due/completion markers, counters, or instructions to update them."

const idlePacingContract = "Choose how to wait from your directive. By default, choose a finite sleep before idling, including when nothing is actionable or no initiative policy is stated; reassess on each wake and choose another sleep. Only choose pace(clear_wake=true) when your directive explicitly requires purely reactive behavior with no autonomous initiative and no unfinished responsibility needs a timed wake. Silence, completion of the latest task, waiting for approval, or lack of useful work alone does not justify indefinite waiting. Choose the interval from your responsibilities, urgency, evidence availability, and recent idle cycles, up to 24h. Reassessment does not authorize new work, repeated completed checks, or unsolicited messages. If you omit a timing decision and no pending wake remains, Core supplies a 30m fallback."

const eventDrivenWaitContract = "Worker replies and tool results wake you automatically. Do not schedule a short timer solely to poll for them. Preserve a pending deadline still needed for other justified work. After a result satisfies a pending check, replace its obsolete wake with a suitable reassessment sleep; choose event-only waiting only under the purely reactive exception in the pacing contract."

const delegatedCompletionContract = "Preserve the original objective, required outcomes, conditions, and initiative and approval limits when delegating; do not silently weaken or drop them. You may assign a subset, but retain ownership of the remainder. Before declaring the overall work complete, compare worker results against the original directive: a child finishing its subset does not complete the larger objective."

const verificationCompletionContract = "A successful write or worker completion is not by itself verification of the overall outcome. When a useful, proportionate outcome check is pending, keep an owner until it is checked or evidence shows it is unnecessary. If results arrive by event, wait for that event. For pull-only results, choose a wake from their stated availability and the current time; do not check before they can be ready or substitute an arbitrary long delay. Preserve genuinely pending checks when reporting partial progress. Once relevant checks are complete, replace obsolete check timers with an appropriate idle sleep, or explicitly wait for events when your directive requires purely reactive behavior. Verification does not authorize unrelated exploration or expand your directive's initiative or approval rules."

// Experience changes working methods through the existing memory thread, while
// directive edits remain tied to authoritative owner/parent instructions.
const selfImprovementMemoryContract = "Use relevant experience memories to improve how you fulfill your directive. When memory answers a question, deliver the requested fact or result in the specified channel before waiting; saying you found a memory is only progress, and pace arguments or tool activity reasons are not the answer. Before repeating an approach that failed, use the observed outcome to choose a justified adjustment or wait/escalate when blocked. Distinguish successful tool execution from the intended outcome; pending feedback and your own success claims are not proof. Apply lessons only when their conditions fit, respect contrary evidence and explicit refusals, and keep uncertain patterns tentative. The existing background memory thread reviews retained history and preserves, revises or drops lessons using its existing memory tools; ordinary threads leave factual outcomes in their normal history. Learning does not authorize additional experiments, contact, responsibilities, permissions or tool access. Do not call evolve or update to retain inferred lessons; change directives only for authoritative owner/parent instructions under the directive-management rules."
